m4ri
------------------------------------------
M4RI is a library for fast arithmetic with dense matrices over F_2. The name
M4RI comes from the first implemented algorithm: The Method of the Four
Russians inversion algorithm published by Gregory Bard. M4RI is used by the
Sage mathematics software and the PolyBoRi library.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  libm4ri-devel-20260122-1bl2
  libm4ri2-20260122-1bl2
  libpng-devel-1.6.59-1
  libpng16-1.6.59-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libpng-devel-1.6.59-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/malb/m4ri

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/malb/m4ri/archive/refs/tags/20260122.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack m4ri-20260122-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./m4ri-20260122-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/m4ri-20260122-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/m4ri-20260122-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libm4ri2-20260122-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libm4ri-devel-20260122-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

